    "result_text": "The full suite is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the GOLD membership tier rule for `POST /api/owners`: `membershipTier` becomes `'GOLD'` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`CountHouseholdMembers.java`** (new function step) \u2014 after `AssignHouseholdId` stamps the shared `householdId` on the new owner and its housemates, this counts existing owners carrying that `householdId` plus the new owner (not yet persisted), and records it on the entity. Owners with no household leave it null. This freezes the count \"after this create,\" per-owner \u2014 consistent with how `namesakeCount`/`bulkSignupWarning` are computed.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `countHouseholdMembers` step between `assignHouseholdId` and `applyRegistrationDate`, under the write transaction.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with accessors.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `membershipTier` expression now returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, else falls back to the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\n5. **Schema files** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 added the `household_size INTEGER` column; fixed hsqldb `data.sql` positional inserts (the other DBs use explicit column lists, so were unaffected).\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
